  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="FR">Output A.1. Enhanced decent work statistics using innovative sources and statistical standards</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="FR">From February 2022 to August 2023, the Ministry of Employment and the National Bureau of Statistics (NBS) established a Labour Market Information System (LMIS) at the national level. The LMIS is adhering to 20th ICLS Resolution in Quarterly Labour Force Survey 2023 and all the relevant labour market indicators are available. 
 
The Government of Seychelles through the National Bureau of Statistics (NBS) also conducted the Population and Housing Census 2022 which adheres to the 19th ICLS resolution on Work, employment and labour underutilization. The NBS also used the ILO Model questionnaire for Census which allows the country to produce labour market statistics from such Census. 
These indicators can be used to improve the production and analysis of information for policy makers and other labour market stakeholders.
 For the LMIS, the ILO has provided technical capacity throughout the whole process  from January 2022 to September 2023. Indeed, the ILO conducted Data Production Workshop to review labour market indicators (source, formula, definition, classification, disaggregation) for all data producers and users in the country in february 2022. The ILO also supported the installation of the LMIS.Stat application software in the LMIS Unit of the National Department of Employment. Moreover, the ILO conducted the Stat management trainings for LMI officials focusing on IT, data and metadata. Furthermore, there was the configuration of structural metadata and initial loading of data. ILO conducted Workshop on SDMX and Data Modelling and has completed all steps necessary for LMIS implementation. 

For the census, the ILO provided technical support by reviewing and contributing towards questionnaire design.</narrative>
   </description>
